---
title: "claimTokenAllocation (LegionFixedPriceSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_supplied: investor invokes claimTokenAllocation(proof, amount, vestingSchedule)
    q_check_supplied --> q_revert_supply: tokens not yet supplied
    q_revert_supply --> [*]: revert TokensNotSupplied
    q_check_supplied --> q_verify_proof: tokens supplied
    q_verify_proof --> q_revert_proof: Merkle proof invalid against claimMerkleRoot
    q_revert_proof --> [*]: revert InvalidProof
    q_verify_proof --> q_check_claimed: proof valid
    q_check_claimed --> q_revert_claimed: position already claimed
    q_revert_claimed --> [*]: revert AlreadyClaimed
    q_check_claimed --> q_check_vesting: not yet claimed
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: vestingSchedule has time-locked portions
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: no vesting required (immediate allocation)
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_vesting: deploy vesting contract; position.vestingContract = newContract
    q_transfer_vesting --> q_mark_claimed: transfer time-locked tokens to vesting contract
    q_direct_transfer --> q_mark_claimed: transfer tokens directly to investor
    q_mark_claimed --> [*]: position.claimed = true; emit TokensClaimed(investor, amount)

    note right of q_verify_proof
        INV-001: Merkle proof must validate against published claimMerkleRoot
        INV-002: Each investor can claim exactly once
    end note

    note right of q_deploy_vesting
        INV-003: Vesting contract deployed per investor for time-locked tokens
        INV-004: Immediate allocations bypass vesting and transfer directly
    end note
